meta {
  name: Create center
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/centers
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{adminToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "Valencia Tech School",
    "country": "ES",
    "taxId": "{{newTaxId}}",
    "payoutIban": "ES9121000418450200051332",
    "platformFeeBasisPoints": 600
  }
}

script:pre-request {
  bru.setVar("newTaxId", "B" + String(Math.floor(10000000 + Math.random() * 89999999)));
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 201) {
    bru.setEnvVar("newCenterId", res.body.id);
  }
}

docs {
  Admin only. `country` is ES or DE; `platformFeeBasisPoints` is at most 3000. `taxId` has its country's shape (ES: a letter or digit, 7 digits and a letter or digit; DE: 9 digits), with or without the prefix, else 422. The center starts as `pending_verification` and the worker checks the VAT number against VIES. Stores the id in `newCenterId`.

  This request sends a random well-formed number, since country and number are unique (reusing the seed's answers 409). With `VIES_MODE=fake` (compose default, offline) 200 is invalid, 300 an outage and any other number valid, so the center becomes active once the worker has checked it. With `VIES_MODE=test` the VIES test service answers 100 as valid, 200 as invalid and anything else as an outage; the seed already uses ES 100, DE 100 and ES 200, so the center stays pending with an `unverified` check. Those three-digit test numbers are accepted as tax ids only in `test` and `fake` modes. The program requests below use the seeded, active Codeworks center either way.
}
